  "summary": "Updates legacy-to-SQLite wallet migration to skip copying legacy records, transactions, and address book entries upfront rather than writing and subsequently deleting them. Address book entries and transactions are instead written directly to their corresponding destination wallets during the migration process. With post-migration record erasure eliminated, several unused wallet database deletion functions (RemoveTxs, EraseTx, DeleteRecordsWithDB, EraseRecords) are removed, and HasLegacyRecords is made static to walletdb.cpp.",
  "problem": "Legacy wallet migration copies all database records into SQLite, only for migration to immediately erase legacy key/script records, delete unneeded address book entries, and overwrite transaction records. This generates redundant disk I/O during migration and requires maintaining otherwise unused database deletion code paths in the wallet.",
  "evidence": [
    "Author description: 'When migrating a legacy wallet, we can skip the records in MigrateToSQLite that we would delete later on during migration... This allows us to remove several database record erase functions, specifically EraseTx and EraseRecords.'"
  ],
